// Outgoing emails found still sending, from the log.
// Backs the "an email may have gone out twice, or not at all" alert: the sending job marks its rows
// sending just before it hands them to the email sender and settles them right after, so a row a
// later claim finds still sending was interrupted in between (a crash, a lost lease, a settle that
// failed). The row is failed rather than sent again, and its recipient may or may not have it. Any
// occurrence is worth a look; a burst points at an instance that keeps dying mid-send.
traces
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
| extend event = tostring(customDimensions["EventName"])
| where event == "OutboxSendInterrupted"
| summarize interrupted = count() by bin(timestamp, 15m)
| where interrupted > 0
